part.text:
The repo root package.json (parent directory, outside workspace) sets "type": "module". So greet.js must use ESM import syntax. I shouldn't inspect the parent dir, but the error tells me it. Let me rewrite greet.js with ESM syntax.

Also note: `__dirname` isn't available in ESM. Use `import.meta.dirname` (Node 20.11+/21.2+). Node v22.19.0 supports `import.meta.dirname`. Or use `new URL('./greeting.txt', import.meta.url)`.

Safer: `path.join(import.meta.dirname, 'greeting.txt')` — Node 22 supports import.meta.dirname. But to be robust, use fileURLToPath(new URL(...)).

Let me rewrite:

```js
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';
import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';

const outputPath = path.join(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), 'greeting.txt');
fs.writeFileSync(outputPath, 'Hello team\n', 'utf8');

console.log(`Wrote ${outputPath}`);
```

No comments. Keep style consistent (no semicolons? original had `console.log('TODO');` with semicolon). Keep semicolons.

